HEADERS WE SHOULD INCLUDE AND WHY

Mandatory
=========
Host:
Connection:

If message has body (Either or - not both!) : 
	Content-Length
		or 
	Transfer Encoding

Optional
========
Expect  : (if sending content the client might want to confirm the request is serveable before sending data)
	
	e.g. Expect: 100-continue (respond with 100 continue, or 401 (Unauthorized) or 405 (Method Not Allowed),)


User-Agent : The "User-Agent" header field contains information about the user agent originating the request, which is often used by servers to help identify the scope of reported interoperability problems, to work around or tailor responses to avoid particular user agent limitations, and for analytics regarding browser or operating system use.
 	 User-Agent = product *( RWS ( product / comment ) )
		product         = token ["/" product-version]
  			product-version = token
 
		e.g. User-Agent: CERN-LineMode/2.15 libwww/2.17b3


